 @dzi333  See above. I'm not regretting without acting, nor sitting on my couch watching YT videos all day. I've been turning down overtime to make sure I have the time and energy to go to the gym regularly, I at least walk for 45-60 minutes every day (with a few exceptions), have changed how I eat quite a bit and have already lost about 10 lbs.

So I'm with you on the whole "regret without corrective action ain't worth much" thing, but I asked and answered that question--what's better for me?--around a month ago. :)

EDIT: Mistyped 20 lbs instead of 10 lbs, and the inspiration of the last 3 months really crystallized, exercise-wise, in the last month, though I was changing my diet and eating habits 3 months ago and taking walks and stuff from Day 1. Just not following a plan.

@eurekaflows thanks 😊 

Yeah sorry I didn’t mean to suggest that you should try to full crimp all the time, it’s just personal preference for me! Some people prefer/feel stronger in other grip types, and sometimes even feel stronger in a 3 finger drag than a full crimp! So definitely try to use whatever grip feels strongest/most comfortable for you, because everyone’s body is built different!

I definitely wouldn’t recommend training full crimp and it’s something that will develop naturally if you body feels like it wants to do it :)
